<title>HONG KONG: Silver Grant interim net down 57.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Silver Grant interim net down 57.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   4.3	 vs 10.1 (see note)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	 vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  8.88 gain vs 20.05 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    7.75	vs 18.29 (see note)</p>
<p>    Turnover		     17.56     vs 20.52 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Silver Grant International</p>
<p>				     Industries Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Silver Grant engages in property leasing, investment holding and share dealing.</p>
<p>The group changed its accounting policy in respect of the recognition of dividend income from investments in 1995 pursuant to the new requirements under Statement of Standard Accounting Practice No. 18. Comparative figures are restated.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of three investment properties at Hong Kong Parkview.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
